**Final submission: T4C — deviation, preferred-level redline at §14.2.2 (validated ok:true, minimality ok).**

What changed this round: I kept the express operative grant ("PB may terminate this Agreement **for convenience, without cause, at any time** upon thirty (30) days' prior written notice to SFJ") and added the verifier's actionable hygiene fix as a second, narrowly scoped replace — the retained ARTICLE 6 carry-over now reads "obtains Regulatory Approval following such termination **or has obtained Regulatory Approval prior to such termination**", so removing the pre-Approval cut-off does not leave that mechanic silent for a post-Approval exit.

Element coverage (all preferred, all in operative text, op 1):
1. Customer convenience termination — gates ($60M spend, pre-Approval window) deleted;
2. 30 days' written notice — blank [***] resolved;
3. Pro rata refund of PB prepayments;
4. Express bar on SFJ convenience termination during the Term.

Untouched and still functioning: the 300% Trial Data Package consideration, Section 11.1.1.4 purchase mechanic, Section 6.2 adjustment, Section 6.7 Buy-Out credit, and every trigger-conditioned SFJ termination right.

Flagged for negotiation rather than redlined: PB's exit is unconditional but not free (300% of Development Costs plus continuing Approval Payments) — the commercial ask is to confirm that amount is consideration for the Trial Data Package and waivable if PB declines to purchase it; and §14.2.10's JSC-disagreement right is near-discretionary in practice if SFJ resists the new no-convenience sentence.
